					</div><!-- class="metadata" -->
					
					
					
					<div class="entry">
						<p>Leaders in the industry and the managers who keep things running need reliable, user-friendly systems in order to get ahead. Half of the battle is knowing where to find quality business management systems. The other half is choosing the right one. The <a title="Viewpoints with Terry Bradshaw" href="https://twitter.com/#!/viewpointstb" target="_blank">Viewpoints with Terry Bradshaw</a> television program features the top operators in the field who are invited on the show to review theirs products and services.  Show host Terry Bradshaw learns about what is available with the audience. The former professional football player and Hall of Fame inductee narrates the program with his usual straightforwardness.</p>
<div id="attachment_59" class="wp-caption alignnone" style="width: 211px"><a href="http://viewpointswithterrybradshaw.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/06/bus-mgmt-solutions-1.jpg"><img src="http://viewpointswithterrybradshaw.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/06/bus-mgmt-solutions-1.jpg" class="size-full wp-image-59" title="viewpoints-terry-bradshaw-business-management-systems" alt="viewpoints-with-terry-bradshaw" width="201" height="250" /></a><p class="wp-caption-text">The best in business management solutions on Viewpoints TV</p></div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Bradshaw was the starring quarterback for the Pittsburgh Steelers who was vital in leading the team to four Super Bowl victories. He earned the “Most Valuable Player” title twice in his 14 year career with the NFL.  He retired in 1984 and has been in sports broadcasting for more than 20 years. He has also written several books, acted in feature films and is a spokesperson for Nutrisystem. His popularity keeps him busy as a motivational speaker and host for Viewpoints TV.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The engaging television program covers topics of interest to business and industry leaders. The Viewpoints Terry Bradshaw show films across the country and airs on regional and national business oriented cable networks. For more information about the program and its host, please visit viewtb.com.</p>
