					</div><!-- class="metadata" -->
					
					
					
					<div class="entry">
						<p>Family health can be one the hardest things to manage in this day and age of larger sized meals and unhealthy snacks at your fingertips. Yet, there are corner stores in small communities that are offering healthy foods for kids and adults alike. Fresh fruit is readily available in most stores including convenience store and gas stations.  The <a title="Viewpoints Terry Bradshaw" href="http://viewpointswithterrybradshaw.net" target="_blank">Viewpoints Terry Bradshaw</a> television program explores the plethora of healthy options available for kids and adults alike.</p>
<div id="attachment_44" class="wp-caption alignnone" style="width: 310px"><a href="http://viewpointswithterrybradshaw.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/05/healthy-snacks.jpg"><img src="http://viewpointswithterrybradshaw.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/05/healthy-snacks-300x199.jpg" class="size-medium wp-image-44" title="viewpoints-terry-bradshaw-family-health" alt="viewpoints-with-terry" width="300" height="199" /></a><p class="wp-caption-text">Family health on the Viewpoints Terry Bradshaw show</p></div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Show host Terry Bradshaw knows how healthy eating can help performance. As a former professional football player, he learned what foods offer protein to help him retain strength and what foods gave him the stamina he needed to play a grueling game of ball. He is a pro ball Hall of Fame inductee who helped steer his team to many championship victories. He retired in 1984 and without regular exercise, gained weight. Recently, Bradshaw became a spokesperson for Nutrisystem, a weight loss program that stresses wellness.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The <a title="Viewpoints with Terry" href="http://viewpointswithterrybradshawtv.mobi" target="_blank">Viewpoints with Terry</a> cable television show covers topics such as lifestyle, business and family matters. The engaging show films in the U.S. and is edited in South Florida. It airs on regional and national business oriented cable networks. More information about the show is at viewtb.com.</p>
